<title>POLAND: ZEW falls 20 pct on bourse debut.</title>
<headline>ZEW falls 20 pct on bourse debut.</headline>
<dateline>WARSAW 1997-05-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>Polish electrodes maker Zaklady Elektrod Weglowych SA (ZEW) started trade on the Warsaw bourse's main market at 36 zlotys, 20 percent below issue.</p>
<p>The company's February initial public offering of 800,000 shares, priced at 45 zlotys per share, was oversubscribed.</p>
<p>-- Warsaw Newsroom +48 22 653 9700</p>
</text>
